  < ---- java.lang.NullPointerException: getMessage and fillInStackTrace ---- >
  << Written from the JDK 28 API specification. getMessage returns the detail
     message given to the constructor. When there is none, a JVM may compute a
     helpful message that names the null expression; the SLeeLa VM does not, so
     the result is null, as on a JVM run with
     -XX:-ShowCodeDetailsInExceptionMessages. fillInStackTrace returns this
     exception, as Throwable does. >>
  public java.lang.String getMessage() { return this.detailMessage; }
  public synchronized java.lang.Throwable fillInStackTrace() { return this; }
